() Tj
T*
(In terms of approaches, the analysis centered on the Discv5 protocol, which is used to) Tj
T*
(establish decentralized handshakes between nodes. The protocol had already been) Tj
T*
(audited in the past and comes as the fifth iteration of the SIL discovery protocol) Tj
T*
(framework. As part of the audit, the protocol?s handshake and wire format were both) Tj
T*
(subject to formal evaluation. This also included exotic XOR-based constructions that the) Tj
T*
(SIL team noted as needing particular attention.) Tj
T*
(The findings encompass two items marked with corresponding severity levels which) Tj
T*
(denote impact of the findings for the connected implementation. These outcomes take) Tj
T*
(on a case of the protocol being rolled out ?as is?. While one concern has only) Tj
T*
(Informational character, the other was evaluated as Medium because of the) Tj
T*
(shortcomings affecting mutual authentication for the bootstrapping nodes.) Tj
T*
(The following sections will first report on the consulting scope and information shared) Tj
T*
(with Cure53 prior to the beginning of the engagement and aimed at supporting analytical) Tj
T*
(tasks. Next, the concerns and observations pertinent to the scope and discussed with) Tj
T*
(the Sila team are documented by Cure53 in a chronological order. The report will) Tj
T*
(then close with a brief conclusion in which the results of this consulting exercise are) Tj
T*
(summarized alongside high-level advice for possible hardening and reinforcement of the) Tj
T*
(existing security guarantees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scope) Tj
T*
