(Miscellaneous Issues) Tj
T*
(This section covers those noteworthy findings that did not lead to an exploit but might aid) Tj
T*
(an attacker in achieving their malicious goals in the future. Most of these results are) Tj
T*
(vulnerable code snippets that did not provide an easy way to be called. Conclusively,) Tj
T*
(while a vulnerability is present, an exploit might not always be possible.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SIL-06-001 Protocol: Limitations in noderecord directory authentication \(Medium\)) Tj
T*
(It was found that the bootstrapping procedure that the Discv5 nodes rely on fails to) Tj
T*
(provide any mutual authentication with regards to the bootstrapping nodes. If the initial) Tj
T*
(bootstrap nodes are compromised, all future decentralized network interaction by the) Tj
T*
(victim?s nodes would be controlled by the attacker.) Tj
T*
(The Discv5 designers are aware of this risk and propose using Node Discovery Via DNS) Tj
T*
(\(SIP-1459\)1 as a potential remedy for the issue. In the case of SIP-1459 deployment,) Tj
T*
(root-signing key communication becomes critical. Therefore, it is best to ship it hardcoded within Discv5) Tj
T*
( clients, with rigid rekeying protocol requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SIL-06-002 Protocol: Pre-shared key support considerations \(Info\)) Tj
T*
(The decentralized use-case for Discv5 cannot be realistically paired with mutual) Tj
T*
(authentication based on long-term keys. However, it is recommended to investigate) Tj
T*
(supporting pre-shared key \(PSK\) features, which could allow nodes to optionally) Tj
T*
(instantiate authenticated connections. This calls for both providing a matching preshared symmetric key.) Tj
T*
(Such features are available in TLS 1.3, where they are used for) Tj
T*
(session resumption2 and in the Noise Protocol Framework, which employs them to) Tj
T*
(improve the authentication security properties of sessions3.) Tj
T*
(Further comparisons have been drawn between Discv5 and certain Noise Handshake) Tj
T*
(Patterns, such as NK4 or IK5. According to the Discv5 designers, the main reason for) Tj
T*
(reticence regarding the use of the Noise Protocol framework stemmed from uncertainty) Tj
T*
(as to whether session IDs can be included within the wire protocol. Despite this, session) Tj
T*
(IDs and other Discv5-relevant materials can be included within a custom data) Tj
T*
(serialization format within the Noise Handshake Protocol payloads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
