(this item of the Sila scope makes a strong impression.) Tj
T*
(To give some details, it can be reiterated that the protocol?s handshake and wire format) Tj
T*
(were both formally examined and the evaluation extended to exotic XOR-based) Tj
T*
(constructions as well. The latter were specifically named as focal points for this) Tj
T*
(assessment by the Sila team. Cure53 made only minor observations about) Tj
T*
(possible improvements and shortcomings that the team responsible for the security of) Tj
T*
(the Discv5 protocol could consider.) Tj
T*
(A call was scheduled with the client to discuss the outcomes as regards handshake) Tj
T*
(authentication, PSK support, bootstrap nodes, key compromise impersonation attacks,) Tj
T*
(XOR constructions, as well as Discv5?s custom wire format. The report follows up on the) Tj
T*
(matters tackled on the call and elaborate on the issues through proper documentation.) Tj
T*
(First, authentication-related findings can be found in SIL-06-001, which additionally) Tj
T*
(offers some comments on mitigations strategies that the SIL team has already been) Tj
T*
(planning. Secondly, SIL-06-002 suggests adding pre-shared key support to the Discv5) Tj
T*
(protocol as an optional measure to reinforce authentication.) Tj
T*
(At this stage, Cure53 has no further concerns to report. In light of the observations made) Tj
T*
(during this late 2019-early 2020 consultancy exercise, Cure53 is happy to report that the) Tj
T*
(Sila Node Discovery Protocol v5 may be seen as sound and robust.) Tj
T*
